1
00:00:37,873 --> 00:00:41,934
[Man] I was sheriff of this county
when I was 25 years old.

2
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:44,035
Hard to believe.

3
00:00:44,112 --> 00:00:47,604
My grandfather was a lawman.
Father too.

4
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:53,453
Me and him was sheriffs at the same
time, him up in Plano and me out here.

5
00:00:53,522 --> 00:00:55,456
I think he's pretty proud of that.

6
00:00:56,591 --> 00:00:58,058
I know I was.

7
00:00:59,661 --> 00:01:03,062
Some of the old-time sheriffs
never even wore a gun.

8
00:01:03,131 --> 00:01:06,760
Folks find that hard to believe.
Jim Scarborough never carried one.

9
00:01:06,835 --> 00:01:08,462
That's the younger Jim.

10
00:01:08,537 --> 00:01:12,997
Gaston Boykins wouldn't wear one
up in Comanche County.

11
00:01:13,074 --> 00:01:16,566
I always liked to hear
about the old-timers.

12
00:01:16,645 --> 00:01:19,637
Never missed a chance to do so.

13
00:01:19,714 --> 00:01:24,276
You can't help but compare yourself
against the old-timers.

14
00:01:24,352 --> 00:01:28,186
Can't help but wonder
how they'd have operated these times.

15
00:01:28,256 --> 00:01:33,125
There's this boy I sent to the electric
chair at Huntsville here a while back.

16
00:01:33,195 --> 00:01:36,528
My arrest and my testimony.

17
00:01:37,766 --> 00:01:41,202
He killed a 14-year-old girl.

18
00:01:41,269 --> 00:01:43,760
Paper said it was a crime of passion,

19
00:01:43,838 --> 00:01:46,705
but he told me there
wasn't any passion to it.

20
00:01:46,775 --> 00:01:51,007
Told me he'd planned to kill somebody
for as long as he could remember.

21
00:01:51,079 --> 00:01:53,980
Said if they turned him out,
he'd do it again.

22
00:01:54,049 --> 00:01:56,643
Said he knew he was going to hell.

23
00:01:56,718 --> 00:01:59,118
Be there in about 15 minutes.

24
00:01:59,187 --> 00:02:01,985
I don't know what to make of that.

25
00:02:02,057 --> 00:02:04,287
I sure do don't.

26
00:02:05,527 --> 00:02:10,089
The crime you see now,
it's hard to even take its measure.

27
00:02:10,165 --> 00:02:12,827
It's not that I'm afraid of it.

28
00:02:13,835 --> 00:02:18,602
I always knew you had to be willing
to die to even do this job.

29
00:02:18,673 --> 00:02:22,973
But I don't want to push
my chips forward and go out

30
00:02:23,044 --> 00:02:26,502
and meet something I don't understand.

31
00:02:30,118 --> 00:02:32,985
A man would have
to put his soul at hazard.

32
00:02:34,589 --> 00:02:36,750
He'd have to say, "OK.

33
00:02:40,795 --> 00:02:42,922
I'll be part of this world."

34
00:02:44,599 --> 00:02:47,363
Yes, sir, I just walked in the door.

35
00:02:47,435 --> 00:02:49,528
He had some sort of thing on him,

36
00:02:49,604 --> 00:02:53,165
like a oxygen tank
for emphysema or something,

37
00:02:53,241 --> 00:02:55,573
and a hose that run down his sleeve.

38
00:02:55,644 --> 00:02:58,169
[Man] Oxygen tank?
What the hell's he got that for?

39
00:02:58,246 --> 00:03:01,010
You got me. Well,
you can look at it when you get in.

40
00:03:01,082 --> 00:03:05,519
- I'll be down there in a bit.
- Yes, sir, I got it under control.

41
00:03:05,587 --> 00:03:07,885
[Grunting]

42
00:03:13,495 --> 00:03:15,656
[Gasping]

43
00:03:24,706 --> 00:03:27,436
[Continues grunting]

44
00:03:35,850 --> 00:03:37,715
[Gasping]

45
00:03:40,021 --> 00:03:42,080
[Sighs]

46
00:04:06,548 --> 00:04:07,845
[Siren sounds]

47
00:04:09,451 --> 00:04:11,043
[Siren blares]

48
00:04:42,317 --> 00:04:46,276
- Howdy. What's this about?
- Step out of the car please, sir.

49
00:04:46,354 --> 00:04:47,548
What is that?

50
00:04:47,622 --> 00:04:49,988
I need you to step out of the car, sir.

51
00:04:57,665 --> 00:04:59,792
- What is that for?
- Would you?

52
00:04:59,868 --> 00:05:02,894
Would you hold still please, sir?

53
00:05:32,734 --> 00:05:34,895
You hold still.

54
00:05:44,212 --> 00:05:45,839
Shit.

55
00:06:41,970 --> 00:06:43,267
[Sighs]

56
00:08:13,995 --> 00:08:15,826
[Fly buzzes]

57
00:09:15,123 --> 00:09:17,057
Agua.

58
00:09:18,493 --> 00:09:20,120
Agua.

59
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,969
Agua.

60
00:09:35,843 --> 00:09:37,811
I ain't got no water.

61
00:09:39,647 --> 00:09:41,945
[Whispers] Agua.

62
00:09:42,016 --> 00:09:44,814
[Panting]

63
00:09:50,024 --> 00:09:51,582
Agua.

64
00:09:53,094 --> 00:09:54,925
I told you I ain't got no agua.

65
00:10:09,877 --> 00:10:11,105
Do you speak English?

66
00:10:13,581 --> 00:10:15,481
Where's the last guy?

67
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:20,283
Ultimo hombre, last man standing. There
must have been one. Where'd he go?

68
00:10:26,627 --> 00:10:29,528
I reckon I go out the way I come in.

69
00:10:29,697 --> 00:10:31,790
[Man speaks Spanish]

70
00:10:32,133 --> 00:10:34,693
Hay lobos.

71
00:10:35,403 --> 00:10:37,132
There ain't no lobos.

72
00:10:51,886 --> 00:10:54,912
[Man] You stopped to watch
your backtrack.

73
00:10:56,457 --> 00:10:58,823
Now shoot my dumb ass.

74
00:11:01,863 --> 00:11:04,696
But if you stop,

75
00:11:04,766 --> 00:11:06,757
you stopped in shade.

76
00:12:41,395 --> 00:12:42,760
[Fly buzzes]

77
00:13:08,923 --> 00:13:10,982
Yeah.

78
00:13:18,332 --> 00:13:20,095
Hmm.

79
00:13:21,469 --> 00:13:23,027
Mmm.

80
00:13:31,879 --> 00:13:35,246
[Thunder rumbles]

81
00:14:17,658 --> 00:14:20,058
My place is wrong?

82
00:14:20,127 --> 00:14:23,722
Yours is the first place
Danzer and Dora will look if they...

83
00:14:23,798 --> 00:14:25,789
If they know.

84
00:14:27,201 --> 00:14:30,898
- What's in the satchel?
- It's full of money.

85
00:14:30,972 --> 00:14:33,202
That would be the day.

86
00:14:33,274 --> 00:14:36,038
- Where'd you get the pistol?
- At the gettin' place.

87
00:14:37,378 --> 00:14:40,541
- Did you buy that gun?
- No. I found it.

88
00:14:42,817 --> 00:14:45,945
- Llewelyn.
- What? Quit your hollering.

89
00:14:46,554 --> 00:14:48,545
What'd you get for that thing?

90
00:14:49,557 --> 00:14:52,924
You don't need to know everything,
Carla Jean.

91
00:14:52,994 --> 00:14:56,395
- I need to know that.
- Keep running that mouth of yours,

92
00:14:56,464 --> 00:14:59,092
I'm gonna take you in the back
and screw you.

93
00:14:59,166 --> 00:15:02,260
- Big talk.
- Keep it up.

94
00:15:02,336 --> 00:15:05,430
Fine. I don't want to know.

95
00:15:05,506 --> 00:15:09,465
I don't even want to know
where you been all day.

96
00:15:09,543 --> 00:15:11,272
That'll work.

97
00:15:25,259 --> 00:15:26,954
All right.

98
00:15:27,728 --> 00:15:29,719
[Water running]

99
00:15:32,733 --> 00:15:35,099
- [Carla Jean] Llewelyn?
- Yeah?

100
00:15:37,405 --> 00:15:40,772
- What're you doing, baby?
- I'm going out.

101
00:15:40,841 --> 00:15:43,002
Going where?

102
00:15:43,077 --> 00:15:45,978
A little something I forgot to do,
but I'll be back.

103
00:15:46,047 --> 00:15:49,380
- And what're you gonna do?
- I'm fixing to do something

104
00:15:49,450 --> 00:15:52,681
dumber than hell, but I'm going anyways.

105
00:15:53,821 --> 00:15:56,289
If I don't come back,
you tell Mother I love her.

106
00:15:57,591 --> 00:15:59,491
Your mother's dead, Llewelyn.

107
00:16:03,631 --> 00:16:05,861
Well, then I'll tell her myself.

108
00:16:06,067 --> 00:16:07,557
[Door closes]

109
00:16:17,178 --> 00:16:19,669
[Engine starts]

110
00:17:17,972 --> 00:17:19,701
[Cocks gun]

111
00:17:29,183 --> 00:17:30,673
[Jingling]

112
00:17:54,742 --> 00:17:57,973
[Thunder rumbles]

113
00:18:05,853 --> 00:18:08,253
[Engine revs]

114
00:18:21,936 --> 00:18:24,871
- [Man shouting indistinct]
- [Grunting]

115
00:18:25,406 --> 00:18:27,374
[Panting]

116
00:18:46,393 --> 00:18:49,294
[Breathing heavily]

117
00:18:53,234 --> 00:18:55,998
[Llewelyn panting]

118
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:57,628
[Gunshot]

119
00:19:02,076 --> 00:19:04,044
[Gunshot]

120
00:19:04,979 --> 00:19:07,777
- [Panicked breathing]
- [Gun cocks]

121
00:19:11,285 --> 00:19:12,912
[Groans]

122
00:19:18,759 --> 00:19:22,217
- [Doors open, close]
- [Men speaking Spanish]

123
00:19:28,035 --> 00:19:31,994
[Dog barking ferociously]

124
00:19:47,254 --> 00:19:48,915
[Panting]

125
00:20:12,646 --> 00:20:14,705
[Snarling, barking]

126
00:20:15,549 --> 00:20:16,880
[Blowing]

127
00:20:21,555 --> 00:20:23,352
- [Yelping]
- [Grunting]

128
00:20:24,191 --> 00:20:26,455
[Panting]

129
00:20:56,623 --> 00:20:58,989
[Footsteps approach]

130
00:20:59,059 --> 00:21:02,392
- How much?
- Sixty-nine cents.

131
00:21:02,463 --> 00:21:03,953
And the gas?

132
00:21:04,031 --> 00:21:06,556
Y'all getting any rain up your way?

133
00:21:07,701 --> 00:21:11,831
- What way would that be?
- Well, I seen you was from Dallas.

134
00:21:13,307 --> 00:21:16,902
What business is it of yours
where I'm from...

135
00:21:17,911 --> 00:21:19,503
...friendo?

136
00:21:21,215 --> 00:21:25,174
- Well, I didn't mean nothing by it.
- You didn't mean nothing?

137
00:21:25,252 --> 00:21:27,618
I was just passing the time.

138
00:21:28,889 --> 00:21:32,757
If you don't want to accept that,
I don't know what else I can do for you.

139
00:21:35,796 --> 00:21:39,232
- Will there be something else?
- I don't know. Will there?

140
00:21:45,639 --> 00:21:47,504
- Is something wrong?
- With what?

141
00:21:47,574 --> 00:21:48,973
With anything.

142
00:21:50,043 --> 00:21:54,207
Is that what you're asking me?
Is there something wrong with anything?

143
00:21:54,281 --> 00:21:57,717
- Will there be anything else?
- You already asked me that.

144
00:22:01,121 --> 00:22:04,648
- Well, I need to see about closing now.
- See about closing?

145
00:22:04,725 --> 00:22:06,659
- Yes, sir.
- What time do you close?

146
00:22:06,727 --> 00:22:08,991
- Now. We close now.
- Now is not a time.

147
00:22:09,062 --> 00:22:13,192
- What time do you close?
- Generally around dark. At dark.

148
00:22:16,270 --> 00:22:19,000
You don't know what
you're talking about, do you?

149
00:22:19,072 --> 00:22:21,165
Sir?

150
00:22:21,241 --> 00:22:24,904
I said you don't know
what you're talking about.

151
00:22:27,281 --> 00:22:29,977
- What time do you go to bed?
- Sir?

152
00:22:30,050 --> 00:22:33,645
You're a bit deaf, aren't you?
I said, what time do you go to bed?

153
00:22:35,389 --> 00:22:37,357
Oh.

154
00:22:37,958 --> 00:22:41,587
Somewhere around 9:30.
I'd say around 9:30.

155
00:22:41,662 --> 00:22:43,220
I could come back then.

156
00:22:43,297 --> 00:22:45,731
Why would you be coming back?
We'll be closed.

157
00:22:45,799 --> 00:22:47,562
Yeah, you said that.

158
00:22:48,802 --> 00:22:53,364
- Well, I got to close now.
- You live in that house out back?

159
00:22:54,241 --> 00:22:57,506
- Yes, I do.
- You lived here all your life?

160
00:22:59,046 --> 00:23:03,176
Well, this is my wife's
father's place, originally.

161
00:23:03,250 --> 00:23:06,879
[Chokes] You married into it?

162
00:23:06,954 --> 00:23:10,856
We lived in Temple, Texas
for many years.

163
00:23:11,758 --> 00:23:14,886
Raised a family there. In Temple.

164
00:23:14,962 --> 00:23:19,058
- We come out here about four years ago.
- You married into it?

165
00:23:19,132 --> 00:23:24,365
- If that's the way you want to put it.
- Well, I don't have some way to put it.

166
00:23:24,438 --> 00:23:26,167
That's the way it is.

167
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:37,181
What's the most you ever lost
on a coin toss?

168
00:23:37,251 --> 00:23:42,245
- Sir?
- The most you ever lost on a coin toss?

169
00:23:42,322 --> 00:23:45,883
Oh, I don't know. I couldn't say.

170
00:23:48,795 --> 00:23:50,285
- Call it.
- Call it?

171
00:23:50,364 --> 00:23:52,491
- Yes.
- For what?

172
00:23:52,566 --> 00:23:53,794
Just call it.

173
00:23:56,236 --> 00:24:00,036
Well, we need to know
what we're calling it for here.

174
00:24:00,107 --> 00:24:03,543
You need to call it.
I can't call it for you.

175
00:24:03,610 --> 00:24:06,704
- Or it wouldn't be fair.
- I didn't put nothing up.

176
00:24:06,780 --> 00:24:10,307
Yes, you did. You've been
putting it up your whole life.

177
00:24:10,384 --> 00:24:12,750
You just didn't know it.

178
00:24:12,819 --> 00:24:15,845
- You know what date is on this coin?
- No.

179
00:24:15,923 --> 00:24:20,223
1958. It's been traveling
22 years to get here.

180
00:24:20,294 --> 00:24:25,027
And now it's here.
And it's either heads or tails.

181
00:24:25,098 --> 00:24:26,463
You have to say. Call it.

182
00:24:26,533 --> 00:24:29,969
Well, look,
I need to know what I stand to win.

183
00:24:30,037 --> 00:24:32,870
- Everything.
- How's that?

184
00:24:32,940 --> 00:24:35,534
You stand to win everything. Call it.

185
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:43,047
All right. Heads, then.

186
00:24:47,888 --> 00:24:49,082
Well done.

187
00:24:51,058 --> 00:24:53,185
- Don't put it in your pocket.
- Sir?

188
00:24:53,260 --> 00:24:56,320
Don't put it in your pocket.
It's your lucky quarter.

189
00:24:56,830 --> 00:24:58,354
Where do you want me to put it?

190
00:24:58,432 --> 00:25:00,559
Anywhere not in your pocket.

191
00:25:00,634 --> 00:25:05,094
Or it'll get mixed in with the others
and become just a coin.

192
00:25:08,108 --> 00:25:09,700
Which it is.

193
00:25:15,482 --> 00:25:17,609
[Rustling]

194
00:25:20,621 --> 00:25:21,952
Llewelyn?

195
00:25:24,758 --> 00:25:26,555
What the hell?

196
00:25:27,761 --> 00:25:30,924
- [Llewelyn] Odessa.
- Why would we go to Odessa?

197
00:25:30,998 --> 00:25:34,434
No, not we. You.
You stay with your mother.

198
00:25:34,501 --> 00:25:35,798
Well, how come?

199
00:25:35,869 --> 00:25:40,135
Look, right now it's midnight Sunday.
Courthouse opens nine hours from now.

200
00:25:40,207 --> 00:25:44,303
Someone's gonna call in the number
on the inspection plate of my truck.

201
00:25:44,378 --> 00:25:46,642
And around 9:30,
they'll show up here.

202
00:25:46,713 --> 00:25:49,273
- How long do we?
- What point would you quit

203
00:25:49,349 --> 00:25:52,546
bothering to look
for your two million dollars?

204
00:25:52,619 --> 00:25:54,814
What am I supposed to tell Mama?

205
00:25:54,888 --> 00:25:57,550
Stand in the door and holler,
"Mama, I'm home!"?

206
00:25:57,624 --> 00:25:59,922
- Llewelyn.
- Come on, pack your things.

207
00:25:59,993 --> 00:26:02,826
Anything you leave,
you ain't gonna see again.

208
00:26:04,097 --> 00:26:08,056
Well, don't fall down apologizing.

209
00:26:08,135 --> 00:26:10,365
Oh, baby, things happen.

210
00:26:11,271 --> 00:26:13,296
Come on, I can't take them back.

211
00:26:36,029 --> 00:26:37,724
Mind riding bitch?

212
00:26:50,610 --> 00:26:52,942
- This his truck?
- Mm-hmm.

213
00:26:57,017 --> 00:26:58,814
Got a screwgie?

214
00:27:01,955 --> 00:27:06,585
- Who cut his tires?
- [Man] Mexicans, I guess. Wasn't us.

215
00:27:07,394 --> 00:27:10,557
- That is a dead dog.
- Yes, it is.

216
00:27:13,767 --> 00:27:16,827
- Where's the receiver?
- I've got it.

217
00:27:17,504 --> 00:27:20,803
These are some ripe petunias.

218
00:27:20,874 --> 00:27:22,739
Hold this, please.

219
00:27:30,517 --> 00:27:32,314
Want it?

220
00:27:34,454 --> 00:27:38,049
- [Man 2] Getting anything on this?
- [Man 3] Not a bleep.

221
00:27:38,125 --> 00:27:39,820
All right.

222
00:27:42,729 --> 00:27:44,321
Give me that.

223
00:27:54,207 --> 00:27:56,835
- I thought it was a car afire.
- It is a car afire.

224
00:27:56,910 --> 00:28:00,368
Wendell said there's something
in the back country too.

225
00:28:00,447 --> 00:28:01,436
Step in there.

226
00:28:01,515 --> 00:28:04,507
When's the county gonna start
paying rent on my horse?

227
00:28:04,584 --> 00:28:07,678
- I love you more and more every day.
- That's very nice.

228
00:28:07,754 --> 00:28:08,948
[Exhales]

229
00:28:09,022 --> 00:28:10,683
- Be careful.
- Always am.

230
00:28:10,757 --> 00:28:12,452
- Don't get hurt.
- Never do.

231
00:28:12,526 --> 00:28:14,391
- Don't hurt no one.
- [Scoffs]

232
00:28:16,663 --> 00:28:18,494
If you say so.

233
00:28:52,766 --> 00:28:56,532
- Wouldn't think a car'd burn like that.
- Yes, sir.

234
00:28:57,237 --> 00:28:58,966
We should've brought wienies.

235
00:28:59,039 --> 00:29:01,974
That look like about
a '77 Ford to you, Wendell?

236
00:29:02,042 --> 00:29:05,273
- It could be.
- I'd say it is. Not a doubt in my mind.

237
00:29:05,345 --> 00:29:10,339
- The old boy shot by the highway?
- Yes, sir. His vehicle.

238
00:29:10,417 --> 00:29:14,615
Man killed Lamar's deputy, took his car,
killed that man on the highway,

239
00:29:14,688 --> 00:29:20,126
swapped for his car, now here it is and
he's swapped again for God knows what.

240
00:29:20,193 --> 00:29:22,593
That's very linear, sheriff.

241
00:29:23,630 --> 00:29:26,827
- Age'll flatten a man, Wendell.
- Yes, sir.

242
00:29:26,900 --> 00:29:28,993
- Then there's this other.
- Yeah.

243
00:29:31,071 --> 00:29:33,266
- You ride Winston.
- You sure?

244
00:29:33,340 --> 00:29:37,606
Oh, I'm more than sure. If anything
happens to Loretta's horse out here,

245
00:29:37,677 --> 00:29:41,135
I can tell you, I don't want
to be the party that was aboard.

246
00:29:41,214 --> 00:29:46,083
It's the same tire tread coming back as
going. Made about the same time too.

247
00:29:46,152 --> 00:29:48,313
You can see the sipes real clear.

248
00:29:50,290 --> 00:29:54,124
Somebody's pried the inspection plate
off the door on this one.

249
00:29:55,328 --> 00:29:57,956
I know this truck.

250
00:29:58,031 --> 00:30:00,591
Belongs to a feller named Moss.

251
00:30:00,667 --> 00:30:03,500
- Llewelyn Moss?
- That's the boy.

252
00:30:03,570 --> 00:30:07,438
- You figure him for a dope runner?
- I don't know.

253
00:30:07,507 --> 00:30:11,273
- I kindly doubt it.
- O.K. Corral is just yonder.

254
00:30:11,344 --> 00:30:13,312
[Flies buzzing]

255
00:30:13,380 --> 00:30:16,110
Oh, hell's bells,
they even shot the dog.

256
00:30:19,085 --> 00:30:21,383
This is just
a deal gone wrong, isn't it?

257
00:30:21,454 --> 00:30:25,720
Yup. Appears to have been
a glitch or two.

258
00:30:29,329 --> 00:30:33,288
- What calibers you got there, sheriff?
- Nine-millimeter.

259
00:30:33,366 --> 00:30:36,494
Couple of.45 ACPs.

260
00:30:36,569 --> 00:30:40,300
Somebody unloaded on that thing
with a shotgun.

261
00:30:42,776 --> 00:30:45,142
How come the coyotes
ain't been at them?

262
00:30:45,211 --> 00:30:47,304
I don't know.

263
00:30:52,118 --> 00:30:55,053
Supposedly, a coyote
won't eat a Mexican.

264
00:30:55,121 --> 00:30:57,589
These boys appear to be managerial.

265
00:30:58,358 --> 00:31:01,953
I think we're looking at more
than one fracas. Execution here.

266
00:31:02,028 --> 00:31:04,428
Wild West over there.

267
00:31:05,398 --> 00:31:09,835
- It's that Mexican brown dope.
- Oh, these boys is all swole up.

268
00:31:09,903 --> 00:31:12,770
So this was earlier.
Getting set to trade.

269
00:31:12,839 --> 00:31:14,704
Then, whoa, differences, and...

270
00:31:16,009 --> 00:31:19,775
- Might not even a been no money.
- That's possible.

271
00:31:19,846 --> 00:31:23,145
- But you don't believe it?
- [Scoffs] No.

272
00:31:23,216 --> 00:31:25,514
Probably I don't.

273
00:31:27,620 --> 00:31:30,248
Well, it's a mess, ain't it, sheriff?

274
00:31:32,092 --> 00:31:35,027
If it ain't,
it'll do till the mess gets here.

275
00:31:47,140 --> 00:31:49,005
[Air hissing]

276
00:33:24,637 --> 00:33:26,332
[Door opens]

277
00:33:28,875 --> 00:33:30,900
[Woman] Yes, sir?

278
00:33:30,977 --> 00:33:35,038
- I'm looking for Llewelyn Moss.
- Did you go up to his trailer?

279
00:33:35,115 --> 00:33:38,016
- Yes, I did.
- Well, I'd say he's at work.

280
00:33:38,084 --> 00:33:41,053
- Do you want to leave a message?
- Where does he work?

281
00:33:41,121 --> 00:33:43,180
I can't say.

282
00:33:44,958 --> 00:33:46,084
Where does he work?

283
00:33:46,159 --> 00:33:50,653
Sir, I ain't at liberty to give out
no information about our residents.

284
00:33:51,798 --> 00:33:52,924
Where does he work?

285
00:33:53,700 --> 00:33:56,032
Did you not hear me?

286
00:33:56,102 --> 00:33:59,162
We can't give out no information.

287
00:34:00,039 --> 00:34:04,305
- [Toilet flushes]
- [Door opens]

288
00:34:18,124 --> 00:34:19,455
[Bus door hissing]

289
00:34:21,294 --> 00:34:25,458
- Why all the way to Del Rio?
- I'm gonna borrow a car from Roberto.

290
00:34:25,532 --> 00:34:29,468
- You can't afford one?
- I don't want to register it.

291
00:34:29,536 --> 00:34:32,232
- Look, I'll call you in a couple days.
- Promise?

292
00:34:32,305 --> 00:34:33,294
Yes, I do.

293
00:34:34,541 --> 00:34:39,410
- I got a bad feeling, Llewelyn.
- I got a good one. Oughta even out.

294
00:34:39,479 --> 00:34:42,880
Listen, you gotta quit
your worrying so much.

295
00:34:42,949 --> 00:34:44,849
- Mama's gonna raise hell.
- Mm-hm.

296
00:34:44,918 --> 00:34:46,909
She's just gonna cuss you up and down.

297
00:34:46,986 --> 00:34:50,786
- Well, you should be used to that.
- I'm used to lots of things.

298
00:34:50,857 --> 00:34:53,826
- I work at Wal-Mart.
- Not anymore, Carla Jean.

299
00:34:53,893 --> 00:34:55,793
You are retired.

300
00:34:55,862 --> 00:34:57,762
- Llewelyn?
- Yes, ma'am?

301
00:34:59,832 --> 00:35:04,496
- You are coming back, ain't you?
- I shall return.

302
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:09,164
[Knocking]

303
00:35:09,242 --> 00:35:11,540
Sheriff's department!

304
00:35:13,546 --> 00:35:15,537
Look at that lock.

305
00:35:17,951 --> 00:35:20,681
- We going in?
- Gun out and up.

306
00:35:24,324 --> 00:35:27,293
- What about yours?
- I'm hiding behind you.

307
00:35:30,330 --> 00:35:32,389
Sheriff's department!

308
00:35:58,157 --> 00:36:01,354
- I believe they done lit a shuck.
- I believe you're right.

309
00:36:01,761 --> 00:36:05,561
- That from the lock?
- Probably must be.

310
00:36:05,632 --> 00:36:09,295
- So when was he here, sheriff?
- I don't know. Oh...

311
00:36:09,369 --> 00:36:11,860
- Now that's aggravating.
- Sheriff?

312
00:36:11,938 --> 00:36:17,843
- Still sweating.
- Oh, sheriff! We just missed him!

313
00:36:18,878 --> 00:36:22,177
We gotta circulate this on radio.

314
00:36:22,248 --> 00:36:23,476
All right.

315
00:36:24,550 --> 00:36:26,609
What do we circulate?

316
00:36:28,855 --> 00:36:32,586
Looking for a man
who has recently drunk milk?

317
00:36:35,328 --> 00:36:39,890
- Oh, sheriff, that's aggravating.
- I'm ahead of you there.

318
00:36:41,868 --> 00:36:45,736
Think this boy Moss has got any notion
of the sorts of sons-of-bitches

319
00:36:45,805 --> 00:36:48,740
- that are hunting him?
- I don't know. He ought to.

320
00:36:52,245 --> 00:36:56,875
He's seen the same things I've seen and
it certainly made an impression on me.

321
00:37:03,156 --> 00:37:05,454
- Take me to a motel.
- Got one in mind?

322
00:37:05,525 --> 00:37:06,787
Someplace cheap.

323
00:37:08,828 --> 00:37:12,389
- [Woman] You tell me the option.
- [Llewelyn] Do what now?

324
00:37:12,465 --> 00:37:16,094
You pick the option
goes with the applicable rate.

325
00:37:16,169 --> 00:37:17,397
[Clears throat]

326
00:37:17,470 --> 00:37:20,667
I'm just one person,
so it don't matter the size of the bed.

327
00:37:22,375 --> 00:37:25,776
- [Paper rustling]
- [Ringing]

328
00:37:26,346 --> 00:37:29,782
[Man on machine] This is Roberto's
Automotive. I'm not in right now.

329
00:37:29,849 --> 00:37:31,578
Please leave a message.

330
00:38:21,701 --> 00:38:23,896
- [Latches case]
- [Clears throat]

331
00:39:24,530 --> 00:39:26,862
[Phone ringing]

332
00:39:30,670 --> 00:39:34,436
- [Woman on phone] Hello?
- Is Llewelyn there?

333
00:39:34,507 --> 00:39:37,943
[Woman] Llewelyn? No, he ain't.

334
00:39:38,010 --> 00:39:39,944
You expect him?

335
00:39:40,012 --> 00:39:43,812
[Woman] Now why would
I expect him? Who is this?

336
00:39:51,390 --> 00:39:54,826
- May I help you?
- Yeah, you got a pair of Larry Mahans?

337
00:39:54,894 --> 00:39:56,259
Shoulder, size 11?

338
00:39:56,329 --> 00:39:58,991
- I'll check.
- You all sell socks?

339
00:39:59,065 --> 00:40:02,557
- Just white.
- Well, white's all I wear. Bathroom?

340
00:40:28,561 --> 00:40:31,826
Don't stop.
Just ride me up past those rooms.

341
00:40:31,898 --> 00:40:35,925
- [Man] What room?
- [Llewelyn] Just drive me around.

342
00:40:36,002 --> 00:40:38,300
I wanna see if someone's here.

343
00:40:45,811 --> 00:40:47,802
Keep going. Don't stop.

344
00:40:47,880 --> 00:40:50,849
[Man] I don't wanna get into
some kind of a jackpot here.

345
00:40:50,917 --> 00:40:52,851
[Llewelyn] It's all right.

346
00:40:52,919 --> 00:40:56,616
[Man] Why don't I just set you down
right here and we won't argue about it?

347
00:40:56,689 --> 00:40:59,988
- Take me to another motel.
- Let's just call it square.

348
00:41:00,059 --> 00:41:03,187
You're in the jackpot,
and I'm trying to get you out of it.

349
00:41:03,262 --> 00:41:05,321
Take me to another motel.

350
00:41:43,970 --> 00:41:45,733
[Bird squawks]

351
00:41:53,980 --> 00:41:56,813
Lab reports from Austin
on that boy by the highway.

352
00:41:56,882 --> 00:41:59,077
- What was the bullet?
- Wasn't no bullet.

353
00:42:00,753 --> 00:42:04,280
- Wasn't no bullet?
- Yes, sir. Wasn't none.

354
00:42:04,357 --> 00:42:09,294
Well, Wendell, with all due respect,
that don't make a lot of sense.

355
00:42:09,362 --> 00:42:10,488
No, sir.

356
00:42:10,563 --> 00:42:14,693
You said entry wound in the forehead,
no exit wound.

357
00:42:14,767 --> 00:42:17,031
- Yes, sir.
- You telling me he shot this boy

358
00:42:17,103 --> 00:42:19,435
and then went digging around
with a knife?

359
00:42:21,040 --> 00:42:23,838
- Sir, I don't wanna picture that.
- I don't either.

360
00:42:23,909 --> 00:42:26,241
Can I freshen that there for you,
sheriff?

361
00:42:26,312 --> 00:42:29,247
Yeah, Maureen, you better had.

362
00:42:29,315 --> 00:42:32,045
Ranger and the DEA
are headed back out to the scene.

363
00:42:32,118 --> 00:42:34,712
Gonna join 'em?

364
00:42:34,787 --> 00:42:37,347
Any new bodies accumulate out there?

365
00:42:38,658 --> 00:42:41,752
- No, sir.
- Well, then I guess I can skip it.

366
00:42:46,732 --> 00:42:48,563
- [Plate clatters]
- [Sighs]

367
00:42:56,242 --> 00:43:00,576
- Twelve-gauge. You need shells?
- Yeah, double-ought.

368
00:43:00,646 --> 00:43:04,480
- Yeah, that'll give you a wallop.
- Y'all got camping supplies?

369
00:43:04,550 --> 00:43:07,849
Tent poles. You already have the tent?

370
00:43:07,920 --> 00:43:09,683
Well, something like that.

371
00:43:09,755 --> 00:43:12,622
Give me the model number on the tent,
I can order poles.

372
00:43:12,692 --> 00:43:15,092
- Never mind. I want a tent.
- What kind?

373
00:43:15,161 --> 00:43:17,152
The kind with most poles.

374
00:43:39,151 --> 00:43:42,211
- Could I get another room?
- You wanna change rooms?

375
00:43:42,288 --> 00:43:44,950
No, ma'am, I wanna keep my room
and get another one.

376
00:43:45,024 --> 00:43:47,515
- Another additional?
- Yes, ma'am.

377
00:43:47,593 --> 00:43:49,959
And do you have a map of the rooms?

378
00:43:50,029 --> 00:43:52,691
Well, yeah, we had a sorta one.

379
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:56,625
Oh, thank you.

380
00:44:00,005 --> 00:44:01,996
How about 38?

381
00:44:02,074 --> 00:44:06,738
Well, you can have the one right next to
yours if you want, 137. It ain't took.

382
00:44:06,812 --> 00:44:10,873
- No, 38 will be fine.
- Well, that's got two double beds.

383
00:44:18,824 --> 00:44:21,156
[Airplane flying overhead]

384
00:44:56,061 --> 00:44:57,585
[Beep]

385
00:45:01,901 --> 00:45:03,027
[Beep]

386
00:45:25,191 --> 00:45:27,819
[Beeping continues]

387
00:46:00,426 --> 00:46:03,327
[Beeping faster]

388
00:46:06,966 --> 00:46:09,628
[Beeping slows]

389
00:46:23,649 --> 00:46:25,879
[Beeping faster]

390
00:46:28,888 --> 00:46:31,288
[Beeping more quickly]

391
00:48:39,618 --> 00:48:41,779
[Air hissing]

392
00:48:44,590 --> 00:48:47,024
[Continues beeping]

393
00:49:42,681 --> 00:49:44,273
[Squeaking]

394
00:49:51,824 --> 00:49:53,917
[Air hissing]

395
00:49:53,992 --> 00:49:56,119
[Clanging]

396
00:49:57,096 --> 00:49:58,893
[Screaming]

397
00:50:38,170 --> 00:50:40,365
[Speaks Spanish]

398
00:50:46,211 --> 00:50:47,508
How'd you find that?

399
00:50:48,480 --> 00:50:50,448
[Speaks Spanish]

400
00:50:55,220 --> 00:50:57,051
[Body thuds]

401
00:52:34,987 --> 00:52:37,888
You shouldn't be doin' that.

402
00:52:37,956 --> 00:52:41,483
Even a young man like you.

403
00:52:41,560 --> 00:52:45,223
- Doin' what?
- Hitchhiking.

404
00:52:51,003 --> 00:52:52,698
Dangerous.

405
00:52:53,538 --> 00:52:58,271
[Elevator dinging]

406
00:53:10,722 --> 00:53:14,249
You know Anton Chigurh by sight,
is that correct?

407
00:53:14,326 --> 00:53:17,853
Yes, sir, I know him every which way.

408
00:53:17,929 --> 00:53:20,295
When did you last see him?

409
00:53:20,365 --> 00:53:21,855
Uh...

410
00:53:21,933 --> 00:53:25,096
...November 28th, last year.

411
00:53:25,170 --> 00:53:28,435
Seem pretty sure of the date.
Did I ask you to sit?

412
00:53:29,241 --> 00:53:33,337
No, sir, but you struck me as a man
who wouldn't wanna waste a chair.

413
00:53:33,412 --> 00:53:38,907
I remember dates, names, numbers.
I saw him November the 28th.

414
00:53:41,053 --> 00:53:42,748
Got a loose cannon here.

415
00:53:42,821 --> 00:53:46,257
We're out a bunch of money,
and the other party is out his product.

416
00:53:46,325 --> 00:53:49,192
- Yes, sir.
- This account will give up

417
00:53:49,261 --> 00:53:53,561
$1,200 in any 24-hour period.
That's up from a thousand.

418
00:53:53,632 --> 00:53:57,796
If your expenses run higher,
I hope you'll trust us for it.

419
00:53:57,869 --> 00:53:59,962
OK.

420
00:54:00,038 --> 00:54:03,804
- Just how well do you know Chigurh?
- What do you wanna know?

421
00:54:03,875 --> 00:54:07,777
I just wanna know your opinion of him,
in general.

422
00:54:07,846 --> 00:54:13,307
- Just how dangerous is he?
- Compared to what, the bubonic plague?

423
00:54:13,385 --> 00:54:15,580
He's bad enough you called me.

424
00:54:15,654 --> 00:54:20,148
Yeah, he's a psychopathic killer,
but so what?

425
00:54:20,225 --> 00:54:22,022
There's plenty of them around.

426
00:54:22,094 --> 00:54:24,790
Killed three men
in a Del Rio motel yesterday,

427
00:54:24,863 --> 00:54:28,458
and two others in that
colossal goat-fuck out in the desert.

428
00:54:28,533 --> 00:54:31,468
- We can stop that.
- Seem pretty sure of yourself.

429
00:54:33,805 --> 00:54:38,105
You've led something of a charmed life,
haven't you, Mr. Wells?

430
00:54:38,176 --> 00:54:43,443
In all honesty, I can't say that charm
has had a whole lot to do with it.

431
00:54:45,117 --> 00:54:47,551
- I was wondering...
- Yes?

432
00:54:48,487 --> 00:54:50,614
Could you validate my parking ticket?

433
00:54:53,024 --> 00:54:57,256
- An attempt at humor, I suppose?
- I'm sorry.

434
00:55:02,033 --> 00:55:07,403
You know, I counted the floors
to this building from the street.

435
00:55:07,472 --> 00:55:09,997
- And?
- There's one missing.

436
00:55:12,978 --> 00:55:14,707
We'll look into it.

437
00:55:34,633 --> 00:55:37,534
One room. One night.

438
00:55:37,602 --> 00:55:41,231
- That'll be $26.
- Alrighty.

439
00:55:45,310 --> 00:55:46,572
You on all night?

440
00:55:46,645 --> 00:55:49,876
Yes, sir, I'll be right here
till 10:00 in the morning.

441
00:55:51,516 --> 00:55:55,976
This here's for you. Now, I ain't
asking you to do anything illegal.

442
00:55:56,054 --> 00:55:59,080
There's someone
who been looking for me. Not police.

443
00:55:59,157 --> 00:56:01,887
You just call me
if anyone else checks in tonight.

444
00:56:01,960 --> 00:56:04,155
And by anyone, I mean any swinging dick.

445
00:56:46,671 --> 00:56:48,798
There just ain't no way.

446
01:00:44,342 --> 01:00:45,468
[Grunts]

447
01:00:54,953 --> 01:00:57,046
- [Glass shatters]
- [Grunts]

448
01:01:11,936 --> 01:01:14,928
[Llewelyn panting]

449
01:01:23,982 --> 01:01:25,381
[Shot fired]

450
01:01:34,292 --> 01:01:36,021
[Groans]

451
01:01:49,507 --> 01:01:51,907
[Panting]

452
01:02:07,659 --> 01:02:09,559
[Car approaching]

453
